/// Calcite's server: reads server.properties, loads the data packs, listens, answers the
/// server list, and logs players in and configures them, starting up, ticking and logging as
/// vanilla's `Main`, `DedicatedServer.initServer` and `MinecraftServer.runServer` do.
///
///     calx run --release src/calcite.calx
///
/// It runs in the folder it's started from, which holds server.properties and server-icon.png,
/// as vanilla's does, and calcite.properties, Calcite's own settings. The first time, it reads the
/// vanilla data from the game's client jar, if the game is installed, or else downloads that part
/// of the jar, and keeps it in cache/, with what it makes of it, which later starts read instead
/// (D140). As with vanilla's `java -D...`, `-Dminecraft.api.env=staging` or
/// `-Dminecraft.api.discovery.host=URL` on its command line picks the Mojang services it uses.
///
/// With `record-inputs=true` in calcite.properties, it records everything it's handed to a new
/// input log in recordings/. `--replay FILE` starts it from the same folder, with what that log
/// recorded where the network, the clock, Mojang's services and the system's random numbers would
/// be, and checks it sends and logs what it did as it was recorded: it says what it found, and
/// fails if it went another way (D21).
///
/// Lines typed into its console run as commands, as vanilla's do. `stop` stops it: it tells its
/// players, waits for them to go, and ends. With `console-dashboard` in calcite.properties, a bar
/// pinned to the terminal shows how it's doing, beside the line commands are typed on.
///
/// `--tick-times FILE` writes, as it ends, when each tick started and how long the server thread
/// worked since the one before, for the bot benchmark (D154). `--stage-times FILE` keeps the
/// seconds the generator's workers have spent in each stage in the file as they go, for the
/// worldgen benchmark (D287). `--rng-tape FILE` writes, as it ends, each value the levels'
/// randoms drew, as the rig's agent writes vanilla's, for `rig/runner/tapediff.py` (D312).
/// `--rng-reseed TIME`, with `level-random-seed` set, seeds each level's random again as it was
/// seeded, the first time the level's tick starts at that game time or later, as the rig's agent
/// does with `reseed`, so the two tapes line up from there (D316). A replay must be given it too.
/// `--entity-trace FILE` writes, as it ends, each mob's state as each of its ticks was done, a line
/// each, as the rig's agent writes vanilla's with `trace`, to line their moves up (CAL-159).
module calcite

